From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pack: honour SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH

The loader header carries the time it was packed, so two packs of the same
inputs never match. Take the time from SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH when it is set, in
UTC, as reproducible builds expect.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/main.cpp
+++ b/main.cpp
@@ -1450,8 +1450,9 @@ static inline rk_time getTime(void) {
 	rk_time rkTime;
 
 	struct tm *tm;
-	time_t tt = time(NULL);
-	tm = localtime(&tt);
+	const char *epoch = getenv("SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH");
+	time_t tt = epoch ? (time_t)strtoll(epoch, NULL, 10) : time(NULL);
+	tm = epoch ? gmtime(&tt) : localtime(&tt);
 	rkTime.year = tm->tm_year + 1900;
 	rkTime.month = tm->tm_mon + 1;
 	rkTime.day = tm->tm_mday;
